# NVIDIA under Proton (checked on an RTX 3080 Ti, driver 620.73.04, with
# Proton Experimental 2026-11-12; see docs/kc-linux-status.md).
#
# NVIDIA cards run 32-lane waves. Console wave64 compute programs that no
# other form brings to 32 lanes are refused by the host ("Required WaveSize
# range [64, 64], but supported range is [32, 32]"); `last` gives those the
# wave-wide form. Offline, 369cbe906ea72764 then builds; 02384a60fda6f2d0
# is still refused (LDS in a group of 128, the mask as data, v_mbcnt,
# v_readlane). Both were also refused on Windows on an RTX 4070 (hyphennn).
VICTORY_WAVE_WIDE=last
#
# The title's own progress watchdog ends a run when its main loop falls far
# behind (a deliberate write to 0 at +0x2215c35, 5m30s into run 27 at 0.1-0.2
# frames a second). Under Proton the frames are that slow; the hook skips it
# (crates/victory-loader/src/hooks.rs). kc-run.sh's own watchdog still ends
# a run that stops.
VICTORY_NO_WATCHDOG=1
